BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Stolen Kisses (1968)
DTSTART:20261029T023000Z
DTEND:20261029T041500Z
DTSTAMP:20261029T023000Z
UID:HK7dlip3HJ
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nNouvelles FemmesTruffaut's alter-
 ego Antoine Doinel (Jean-Pierre Léaud) gains access to the hearts of Pari
 s by becoming a detective. He’s emotionally up and down with his girlfri
 end Christine (Claude Jade) but the endearingly hapless fellow is instantl
 y smitten by the elegant wife (Delphine Seyrig) of a client.\n\nhttps://ww
 w.siff.net/programs-and-events/nouvelles-femmes/stolen-kisses\n\nEstimated
  start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Man and A Woman (1966)
DTSTART:20261105T033000Z
DTEND:20261105T053000Z
DTSTAMP:20261105T033000Z
UID:ymZEn68mqm
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 102 mins (1h42m)\n\nNouvelles Femmes60th Anniversary
  Screening. A man (Jean-Louis Trintignant) and a woman\, (Anouk Aimée)\,
  who’ve painfully lost their loves\, meet by chance. They’re very appe
 aling to each other (and to us)\, but can current attraction overcome past
  memories? Aimee’s enigmatic face has answers. This film played for 82 s
 traight weeks in Seattle.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/nouv
 elles-femmes/a-man-and-a-woman\n\nEstimated start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Discreet Charm of the Bourgeoisie (1972)
DTSTART:20261110T023000Z
DTEND:20261110T043000Z
DTSTAMP:20261110T023000Z
UID:raujo4vZk7
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 102 mins (1h42m)\n\nSIFF Movie Club 4K restoration.
  A group of six friends - three men and three women decidedly of the Frenc
 h Upper Middle Class - have their dinner plans continually interrupted due
  to a series of bizarre events that can only be described as Buñuelian. I
 ntro by Graphic Design Manager Rhys Iliakis.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/progr
 ams-and-events/siff-movie-club/the-discreet-charm-of-the-bourgeoisie\n\nEs
 timated start: 18:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pierrot le Fou (1965)
DTSTART:20261111T033000Z
DTEND:20261111T053500Z
DTSTAMP:20261111T033000Z
UID:2Iwpxo12vu
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 110 mins (1h50m)\n\nNouvelles FemmesA husband (Jean-
 Paul Belmondo) flees his shallow Paris life with the babysitter (Anna Kari
 na)\, to French Riviera escapades with gangsters\, stolen loot\, sunny hed
 onism\, political commentary\; a charming disorder\, a reflection of direc
 tor Godard's and Karina’s stormy marriage. It’s truly moving when he h
 as her gaze into our/his camera’s eyes.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs
 -and-events/nouvelles-femmes/pierrot-le-fou\n\nEstimated start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:My Night at Maud's (1969)
DTSTART:20261118T033000Z
DTEND:20261118T053000Z
DTSTAMP:20261118T033000Z
UID:iFjuR2vZHl
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 105 mins (1h45m)\n\nNouvelles FemmesFate and chance 
 entwine as a man (Jean-Louis Trintignant)\, convinced he’ll marry a woma
 n he’s never met (Marie-Christine Barrault)\, is unexpectedly side-track
 ed into an evening with Maud (Françoise Fabienne)\, a desirable paragon o
 f education\, culture\, challenging conversation\, career stability\, and 
 bedroom eyes.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/nouvelles-femmes
 /my-night-at-mauds\n\nEstimated start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beavis and Butt-Head Do America (1996)
DTSTART:20261204T030000Z
DTEND:20261204T044000Z
DTSTAMP:20261204T030000Z
UID:VtN4Vm440u
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 81 mins (1h21m)\n\nWaking to discover their beloved 
 television set has been stolen\, dimwitted delinquents Beavis and Butt-Hea
 d leave their squalid dwellings to embark on a couch potato road trip in t
 he hopes to finally score.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/the
 -open-road/beavis-and-butt-head-do-america\n\nEstimated start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Twilight (2008)
DTSTART:20261207T000000Z
DTEND:20261207T022500Z
DTSTAMP:20261207T000000Z
UID:QUYCxEONDN
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 127 mins (2h07m)\n\nSIFF Book ClubIt's time to get c
 ozy this winter with Twilight! We're reading (or rereading for the umptee
 nth time) Stephenie Meyer's bestselling novel and then watching (or rewatc
 hing for the zillionth time) Catherine Hardwicke's adaptation\, presented 
 in 35mm. Arrive early to check out Beguiled Books’ swoon-worthy selectio
 ns and local artist Chloe Ladwig’s Cullen-approved prints. Forever Twili
 ght in Forks will be joining us too! Chat with them in the lobby to learn 
 more about their festival and collection.  In recognition of the flawed w
 ay in which the “Twilight” book and film series depict the Quileute Tr
 ibe\, we're donating a portion of ticket proceeds to the Quileute Move to 
 Higher Ground Project\, and we encourage you to do the same to the extent 
 that you are able.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/siff-book-c
 lub/twilight\n\nEstimated start: 16:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Damnation (1988)
DTSTART:20261208T023000Z
DTEND:20261208T044500Z
DTSTAMP:20261208T023000Z
UID:BD8AgxDk8B
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 116 mins (1h56m)\n\nSIFF Movie Club4K restoration. A
  mid-career masterwork by legendary Hungarian art house auteur Béla Tarr 
 and the first of his internationally acclaimed trilogy of films written in
  collaboration with author László Krasznahorkai (including the legendary
  Sátántangó).Intro by Cinema Worker Adam Plesser.\n\nhttps://www.siff.n
 et/programs-and-events/siff-movie-club/damnation\n\nEstimated start: 18:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
